WEBVTT

00:00:00.201 --> 00:00:01.368
Previously on The O.C.:

00:00:01.576 --> 00:00:03.786
Julie and Caleb's wedding invitation.
Getting married in...

00:00:03.995 --> 00:00:05.871
- Two weeks.
- Wow. They're really doing it.

00:00:06.079 --> 00:00:08.414
I know it should be simple.
Your boyfriend hits you...

00:00:08.623 --> 00:00:10.749
...you leave him. Right?
- It's never simple.

00:00:10.957 --> 00:00:14.710
You're probably a fan of the classics.
Superman? No? Batman?

00:00:14.918 --> 00:00:18.629
You probably really need Ryan right now.
Me being here, I'm getting in the way.

00:00:18.837 --> 00:00:21.339
- It's more than twice what we put into it.
- Caught me at a good time.

00:00:21.547 --> 00:00:24.883
- He's up to something.
- I don't care. $2.5 million.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.967
You and me, we're gonna be fine.

00:00:32.512 --> 00:00:34.139
Ryan.

00:00:34.347 --> 00:00:36.932
Ryan, hey. Hey, man, are you asleep?

00:00:42.352 --> 00:00:43.561
Ryan.

00:00:44.895 --> 00:00:48.522
Ryan. Are you asleep?
Yeah, I can't sleep either.

00:00:48.731 --> 00:00:52.775
I know what you're gonna say. You know,
she hasn't technically dumped me yet...

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:55.610
...but it's only a matter of time, right?
So, what do I do?

00:00:55.777 --> 00:00:58.195
Do I force a confrontation
or do I just continue...

00:00:58.404 --> 00:01:02.114
...to be whiny and passive-aggressive
until she realizes what a catch I am?

00:01:03.115 --> 00:01:04.324
Ryan?

00:01:04.532 --> 00:01:07.034
- Ryan, Ryan, Ryan. You asleep?
- Yeah.

00:01:07.243 --> 00:01:09.369
Sorry.
I'm gonna let you go back to sleep, okay?

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.162
As bad as things are for me,
they're worse for you.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.371
What?

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.040
I'm at least in my own bed not sleeping.
You're on my floor not sleeping.

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:20.543
- Because you won't stop talking.
- But also because your ex-girlfriend...

00:01:20.751 --> 00:01:23.795
...is sleeping in your room,
to the dismay of your girlfriend.

00:01:24.003 --> 00:01:26.088
- Marissa's fine with it.
- I'm sure she is.

00:01:26.296 --> 00:01:29.506
The same way you'd be fine with it if
Oliver was sleeping on her couch.

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:30.716
It's cool.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.717
What, you want me to kick Theresa out?

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:36.219
No. But aren't you just the least bit
curious as to when she's leaving?

00:01:36.427 --> 00:01:38.220
No, I'm not. I'm not worried about it.

00:01:38.429 --> 00:01:39.471
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:43.223
Good. Night. Go back to bed.
Or the floor.

00:01:54.772 --> 00:01:57.107
- I should talk to Theresa.
- Let me come with you.

00:02:00.484 --> 00:02:03.152
- Theresa?
- Housekeeping.

00:02:03.361 --> 00:02:06.363
- Hello?
- Maybe she's still at work.

00:02:06.571 --> 00:02:09.156
- Her bag's here.
- Yeah. Apparently, she's been shopping.

00:02:12.909 --> 00:02:14.910
Sorry. I didn't hear you guys come in.

00:02:15.118 --> 00:02:18.412
Let me know if you ever need anything.
My mom's got lots of toiletries.

00:02:19.704 --> 00:02:23.373
Thanks, but I'm probably not
gonna be here that much longer.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.625
You're not?

00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:28.752
No, I can't impose
on Seth's parents forever.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.628
- Sure you can. I intend to.
- Thanks...

00:02:30.836 --> 00:02:35.047
...but I really need to figure things out.
I have some family I can call, so...

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.425
So see you tomorrow?

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:42.052
No. I picked up a morning shift
at the bakery, so...

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.470
Oh, all right. So maybe after school?

00:02:45.346 --> 00:02:49.848
- Sure. But aren't you and Marissa...?
- Yeah. No, I mean we'll both see you.

00:02:50.057 --> 00:02:54.435
We'll all see you, because my girlfriend's
currently dating her father, which to me...

00:02:54.643 --> 00:02:56.811
- Seth.
- We'll talk about this tomorrow.

00:02:57.019 --> 00:02:58.979
- Good night.
- Good night.

00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:02.481
All right, good night.

00:03:02.898 --> 00:03:04.149
Night.

00:03:58.891 --> 00:04:02.352
So, what's it gonna be, Cal?
The Hyatt Newporter?

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.479
The pool at the Four Seasons Hotel
where everybody gets married?

00:04:05.687 --> 00:04:08.356
Or the beautiful glass cathedral
overlooking the ocean...

00:04:08.564 --> 00:04:10.190
...at the Wayfarer's Chapel?

00:04:13.943 --> 00:04:16.194
I have to get to work.

00:04:16.402 --> 00:04:18.987
Whatever you like, Juju.

00:04:20.322 --> 00:04:21.572
Sorry about breakfast, Kiki.

00:04:21.781 --> 00:04:25.742
Dad, the only reason we're having
this breakfast is so we can do some work.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.827
You have been so busy with the wedding,
I haven't even seen you.

00:04:29.035 --> 00:04:33.163
Every time I've asked him to help me
with the wedding, he says he's with you.

00:04:33.371 --> 00:04:36.498
Really? So, CayCay,
what have you been doing all this time?

00:04:36.707 --> 00:04:38.166
Don't you have someplace to be?

00:04:38.374 --> 00:04:40.709
As a matter of fact,
I'm meeting Jimmy for breakfast.

00:04:40.918 --> 00:04:43.294
I bet even that sounds pretty good
to you right now.

00:04:43.503 --> 00:04:45.170
The Wayfarer Chapel it is.

00:04:45.379 --> 00:04:49.173
Well, are you sure? I mean, these photos
don't really do it justice. You know what?

00:04:49.381 --> 00:04:52.008
I should take you up there this weekend,
you'll love it.

00:04:52.216 --> 00:04:53.968
I wish I could. I'm out of town.

00:04:54.176 --> 00:04:57.178
What? Since when? You can't go.
We're getting married next week.

00:04:57.386 --> 00:04:59.638
Just one night. Business.

00:04:59.846 --> 00:05:01.931
Business where?

00:05:02.139 --> 00:05:05.183
- Nevada.
- Nevada. As in Las Vegas, Nevada?

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:08.143
- Actually...
- You're going out of town for one night...

00:05:08.352 --> 00:05:11.020
...to Vegas on business? What business?

00:05:11.187 --> 00:05:12.354
There is no business.

00:05:12.563 --> 00:05:15.648
You're going to Vegas
because you're having a bachelor party.

00:05:15.856 --> 00:05:18.233
- Some of the investors and I are...
- Hiring strippers...

00:05:18.441 --> 00:05:22.027
...drinking too much and gambling all
night the weekend before our wedding?

00:05:22.235 --> 00:05:24.904
It sounds like a bachelor party to me.

00:05:25.112 --> 00:05:28.156
I have to admit,
I feel a little hurt that I wasn't invited.

00:05:28.364 --> 00:05:30.866
- Yeah, me too.
- Not that I have any affection for you.

00:05:31.074 --> 00:05:33.784
You know that. But I do love the Vegas.

00:05:33.993 --> 00:05:37.620
- I didn't know you love the Vegas, Dad.
- I love the Vegas. I love the Vegas.

00:05:37.828 --> 00:05:39.538
Ryan, how do you feel about the Vegas?

00:05:39.746 --> 00:05:42.123
Never been to the Vegas.
Mom was all about the Reno.

00:05:42.331 --> 00:05:45.458
Dad, we should go. You love Vegas.
Ryan and I have never been.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:48.668
He can use his mutant
card-counting abilities to pay for the trip.

00:05:48.877 --> 00:05:51.837
- Sounds like fun for the whole family.
- What about Theresa?

00:05:52.046 --> 00:05:54.547
Well, I can take care of Theresa.
You guys should go.

00:05:54.756 --> 00:05:56.965
Do I have any say in this?

00:05:57.174 --> 00:05:58.550
No.

00:05:59.175 --> 00:06:01.135
Enjoy your bachelor party.

00:06:12.558 --> 00:06:14.143
Hey. Ready for breakfast?

00:06:14.351 --> 00:06:17.603
Almost. My realtor is on her way.
I just have to give her the contract.

00:06:17.812 --> 00:06:18.979
Contract for what?

00:06:19.187 --> 00:06:20.772
Well, with any luck...

00:06:22.064 --> 00:06:23.440
...my new house.

00:06:24.107 --> 00:06:26.192
Jimmy, it's right on the beach.
It's perfect.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.235
I want to give Marissa a home
she can be proud of. You know?

00:06:29.402 --> 00:06:31.612
What are you gonna do
with your half of Caleb's money?

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.697
I'm taking some of it
to Vegas this weekend.

00:06:33.905 --> 00:06:37.240
The boys and I are crashing
his bachelor party. You want to come?

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:41.285
Are you kidding? The man bailed us out,
took Julie off my hands.

00:06:41.493 --> 00:06:43.036
I'll buy him his first lap dance.

00:06:43.411 --> 00:06:48.206
Hell, I'll give him one myself. Can you
grab that? I just gotta get the contract.

00:06:51.166 --> 00:06:53.584
Hi. Gail van Deepen. You must be Sandy.

00:06:53.792 --> 00:06:55.877
- Yeah.
- Congratulations on selling the restaurant.

00:06:56.086 --> 00:06:57.378
You must have made a fortune.

00:06:57.586 --> 00:07:00.880
I heard Robert Campbell is gonna turn
that area into an outdoor mall.

00:07:01.089 --> 00:07:03.757
Robert Campbell?
We sold the restaurant to Caleb Nichol.

00:07:03.965 --> 00:07:07.926
Then I guess Caleb is gonna make
a fortune. Well, another fortune, right?

00:07:08.135 --> 00:07:12.179
But you and Jimmy must have made good
money. What are you gonna do next?

00:07:13.346 --> 00:07:15.014
I wanna kill him.

00:07:15.223 --> 00:07:17.682
Then I'd probably go to jail,
but it would be better...

00:07:17.891 --> 00:07:20.351
...than having to move in
with him and my mom, right?

00:07:20.559 --> 00:07:22.936
That way, I won't have to tell my dad
I'm moving out.

00:07:23.144 --> 00:07:24.603
You still haven't told him?

00:07:25.479 --> 00:07:27.772
What am I supposed to say,
that Caleb's blackmailing me?

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.524
My dad'll kill him
and I'll have to move in with my mom.

00:07:30.732 --> 00:07:32.275
So, what are you gonna tell him?

00:07:32.775 --> 00:07:35.777
I don't know, but I guess
I have to do it by this weekend, huh?

00:07:35.985 --> 00:07:38.070
Your dad might be going
to Vegas this weekend.

00:07:38.279 --> 00:07:39.821
How do you know?

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:42.490
Because I might be going
to Vegas this weekend.

00:07:42.698 --> 00:07:43.990
For what?

00:07:44.199 --> 00:07:45.908
- Caleb's bachelor party.
- What?

00:07:46.117 --> 00:07:49.285
With, like, strippers and prostitutes
and showgirls?

00:07:49.494 --> 00:07:51.870
I don't know, I hope so.
What? No. I'm not gonna go.

00:07:52.079 --> 00:07:53.913
I can't leave Theresa here by herself.

00:07:54.122 --> 00:07:56.081
Theresa? What about me?

00:07:57.249 --> 00:07:59.792
You know what I mean.
You got Summer and your sister.

00:08:00.001 --> 00:08:01.793
Theresa, she's got nobody.

00:08:02.294 --> 00:08:03.878
Well, she's got me.

00:08:04.462 --> 00:08:07.589
I mean, I am your girlfriend, right?

00:08:09.632 --> 00:08:13.592
So, I mean, any friend of yours
is a friend of mine.

00:08:13.801 --> 00:08:15.385
Right?

00:08:21.389 --> 00:08:24.349
- You are my girlfriend.
- Glad to hear it.

00:08:25.975 --> 00:08:30.228
- Now, about those strippers...
- What strippers? I don't know of any stri...

00:08:30.436 --> 00:08:32.896
I don't want Chippendales.
I want strippers.

00:08:33.105 --> 00:08:36.065
Full-on, full-frontal male strippers.

00:08:36.273 --> 00:08:39.108
Preferably at a place
that serves bottomless margaritas.

00:08:40.276 --> 00:08:43.194
Or I could invite the girls over
and I could throw you...

00:08:43.403 --> 00:08:45.904
...a lovely,
catered bachelorette cocktail party.

00:08:46.113 --> 00:08:48.614
- With strippers.
- Without strippers.

00:08:48.823 --> 00:08:51.408
Julie, we are smart, sophisticated women.

00:08:51.616 --> 00:08:56.244
We don't need strange, naked men
dancing in front of us to be entertained.

00:08:58.996 --> 00:09:02.164
I'm not as smart as you.
Plus, the boys are getting strippers.

00:09:02.373 --> 00:09:04.374
The boys are not getting strippers.

00:09:04.583 --> 00:09:08.460
Kirsten, it's Las Vegas. You get strippers
as a side with your entr Áe.

00:09:09.044 --> 00:09:12.296
They're getting strippers. Why else
would Sandy go to Vegas with Caleb?

00:09:12.504 --> 00:09:13.880
Strippers, huh?

00:09:14.047 --> 00:09:16.173
Get all the Newpsies into limos,
drive to L. A...

00:09:16.382 --> 00:09:18.716
...have dinner on Sunset,
then head south to Mantopia.

00:09:18.925 --> 00:09:20.968
- Or the Stud Farm.
- You've done research.

00:09:21.176 --> 00:09:24.970
Todd in Accounting, who also told me
about this place called The Petting Zoo.

00:09:25.179 --> 00:09:26.763
It's not exactly legal, but...

00:09:26.972 --> 00:09:29.890
Julie, I am not going to a place
called The Petting Zoo.

00:09:30.098 --> 00:09:31.766
You don't know where the pets
have been.

00:09:32.016 --> 00:09:33.476
We'll be too drunk to care.

00:09:33.684 --> 00:09:37.728
- No strippers.
- Just one stripper? Please?

00:09:37.937 --> 00:09:40.605
Just one little stripper
who never hurt anyone...

00:09:40.772 --> 00:09:43.190
...who's just trying to make his way
in the world?

00:09:43.732 --> 00:09:45.441
Naked.

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.359
One little stripper.

00:09:47.776 --> 00:09:49.069
Yes! You're the best.

00:09:50.278 --> 00:09:52.029
But no Chippendales.

00:09:52.404 --> 00:09:54.447
And not little.

00:09:55.906 --> 00:09:57.115
A bachelor party?

00:09:57.741 --> 00:10:00.409
Where really anything could happen.

00:10:01.118 --> 00:10:02.327
Good to know.

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:04.495
Yeah. Just kind of
a courtesy thing, really.

00:10:04.703 --> 00:10:07.914
Seeing as how, last time I checked,
we're still boyfriend and girlfriend.

00:10:08.122 --> 00:10:12.583
Even though you've been ignoring me in
the halls and don't return any of my calls.

00:10:12.792 --> 00:10:14.460
I didn't mean for that to rhyme.

00:10:15.127 --> 00:10:17.128
- Look, Cohen...
- I just want you to tell me...

00:10:17.336 --> 00:10:20.547
...that you're not gonna let
what your dad thinks of me break us up.

00:10:26.592 --> 00:10:28.260
- He's my dad.
- So what?

00:10:28.468 --> 00:10:32.679
Summer, I don't care about your dad.
Okay? I care about you a lot.

00:10:32.846 --> 00:10:34.847
And if that's not good enough for you...

00:10:36.765 --> 00:10:39.809
Obviously, that's not good enough
for you, so I'll go to Vegas.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.603
Wait.

00:10:48.648 --> 00:10:50.649
- Hi.
- Hey.

00:10:50.857 --> 00:10:52.525
How was work? How you feeling?

00:10:52.733 --> 00:10:56.861
Good. I'm actually going back.
I picked up another shift tonight.

00:10:57.070 --> 00:11:00.030
Marissa and I were kind of hoping
we could all hang out.

00:11:00.488 --> 00:11:04.699
Yeah, I can't. I have to make money
if I'm gonna go to Atlanta.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:08.160
- Atlanta?
- Yeah, my cousin Kim lives in Atlanta.

00:11:08.368 --> 00:11:11.203
She said I can go stay with her
as long as I pay my own way.

00:11:13.413 --> 00:11:16.623
I mean, she doesn't have
a pool house or anything...

00:11:16.957 --> 00:11:19.625
...but that way,
maybe I can get a second chance too.

00:11:22.627 --> 00:11:24.462
How much you need?

00:11:30.215 --> 00:11:31.383
I can't take your money.

00:11:34.259 --> 00:11:37.637
- I don't even... Two thousand dollars?
- I'll ask the Cohens.

00:11:37.845 --> 00:11:39.137
No, you won't.

00:11:39.846 --> 00:11:42.723
Listen to me.
This is not your problem, okay?

00:11:43.432 --> 00:11:46.184
Go. Win. Make money.

00:11:46.392 --> 00:11:47.976
That's what I'm gonna do.

00:11:56.857 --> 00:11:58.816
Two thousand dollars, huh?

00:11:59.025 --> 00:12:01.151
Well, I've got about...

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.987
I'd say I've got about a thousand
in savings bonds, bar mitzvah bucks.

00:12:05.195 --> 00:12:06.821
I could throw in a couple hundred.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.573
I can't ask you guys to do that.

00:12:08.739 --> 00:12:10.365
You didn't ask. We volunteered.

00:12:11.032 --> 00:12:12.658
Thanks, but it's still not enough.

00:12:12.867 --> 00:12:16.411
You could make it enough. Take that
money to Vegas and triple it at blackjack.

00:12:16.619 --> 00:12:19.371
It's been a while
since I've done the card-counting thing.

00:12:19.538 --> 00:12:23.207
Listen, I'm gonna start you off slow.
If you suck, I'm just gonna cut you off.

00:12:24.583 --> 00:12:27.876
- How do we get in the casinos?
- I think we'd use our fake IDs.

00:12:28.085 --> 00:12:30.920
- You have fake IDs?
- C.D. Sebulski, it's good to meet you.

00:12:31.128 --> 00:12:33.630
- Have you met Marty Nayfis?
- Oh, God.

00:12:34.756 --> 00:12:38.341
Okay, look, you guys go to Vegas.
I'll take care of Theresa.

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:43.386
If you win, great. If not,
well, then Theresa never has to know.

00:12:44.845 --> 00:12:47.930
- What do you have to lose?
- Just $ 1000 in bar mitzvah bonds.

00:12:48.139 --> 00:12:49.765
But other than that, nothing.

00:12:50.182 --> 00:12:51.850
You in?

00:12:52.392 --> 00:12:54.643
Marty, are you in?

00:12:57.812 --> 00:12:58.979
I'm in.

00:13:25.829 --> 00:13:29.039
- I love the Vegas.
- Reno was never like this.

00:13:37.295 --> 00:13:38.837
What is this place?

00:13:39.004 --> 00:13:43.632
This is the Hard Rock Hotel and Casino.
According to Seth, it's ground zero...

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.008
...for aging hipsters like yourself.

00:13:47.509 --> 00:13:49.135
I thought we were going to Caesar's.

00:13:49.344 --> 00:13:51.929
Caesar's didn't have
a permanent Springsteen exhibit.

00:13:52.137 --> 00:13:53.888
Although they do have Celine Dion.

00:13:54.097 --> 00:13:55.556
Yet another reason we're here.

00:13:55.723 --> 00:13:59.433
- Mock if you must, but she can sing.
- You're gonna regret saying that...

00:13:59.642 --> 00:14:01.768
...on your birthday.
- Yeah, really.

00:14:01.977 --> 00:14:03.770
Welcome to Hard Rock.
My name is Amy.

00:14:03.978 --> 00:14:05.729
Which one of you is Mr. Cohen?

00:14:05.938 --> 00:14:08.606
Hi, Amy, we spoke on the phone.
It's good to see you.

00:14:08.773 --> 00:14:11.733
Yes, good to see you. We have
the penthouse all ready for you.

00:14:11.941 --> 00:14:13.234
If you will follow me.

00:14:13.442 --> 00:14:15.485
- Penthouse?
- Yeah.

00:14:15.694 --> 00:14:18.570
- So whose card did you put that on?
- Oh, please, the old man's.

00:14:18.779 --> 00:14:20.655
Oh, I love you, son. I love you.

00:14:20.864 --> 00:14:22.406
I love you too, Dad.

00:14:23.115 --> 00:14:24.866
Just not as much as I love Vegas.

00:14:25.075 --> 00:14:27.826
The casino, restaurants, pool and spa
are all on this level.

00:14:28.035 --> 00:14:30.578
And if you'll follow me,
I'll show you our bowling alley.

00:14:30.786 --> 00:14:32.329
God, there's a bowling alley?

00:14:32.496 --> 00:14:35.039
Yes, sir. It's in your room.

00:14:36.457 --> 00:14:37.666
Did you see that?

00:14:37.874 --> 00:14:40.709
I just almost bowled a strike.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:44.045
In our hotel room, man.
I'm never going home.

00:14:49.215 --> 00:14:51.007
It's like a million-dollar frat house.

00:14:51.216 --> 00:14:53.676
I know. It's fantastic.

00:14:54.593 --> 00:14:56.469
Well, I'm gonna explore the casino.

00:14:56.678 --> 00:14:58.345
May I give you gentlemen a tour?

00:14:58.554 --> 00:15:00.180
No, I'll find my way. Thanks.

00:15:00.388 --> 00:15:03.140
- We're good. Thanks, Amy.
- Thanks.

00:15:04.432 --> 00:15:08.018
Actually, you know what?
We'll take that tour.

00:15:08.768 --> 00:15:11.187
Sure. I just need to see some ID.

00:15:12.396 --> 00:15:15.981
It's just a formality. We have
a lot of kids under 21 using fake IDs...

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:20.568
...to get onto the casino floor. We'd hate
to have to throw them out of the hotel.

00:15:21.151 --> 00:15:23.694
You know what? I don't think
we're gonna need that tour.

00:15:23.903 --> 00:15:25.862
- But thank you for stopping by.
- Absolutely.

00:15:26.071 --> 00:15:27.530
Really sweet.

00:15:31.032 --> 00:15:34.326
What are we gonna do? I don't
wanna get thrown out. I love the hotel.

00:15:34.535 --> 00:15:36.161
- Me too.
- I wanna marry the hotel...

00:15:36.369 --> 00:15:38.329
...and have gambling-addicted,
alcoholic kids.

00:15:38.537 --> 00:15:40.872
- We'll find another casino.
- What, a youth casino?

00:15:42.456 --> 00:15:43.665
Seth, it's Vegas.

00:15:43.874 --> 00:15:47.334
You wanna find some action in this town,
all you gotta do is ask.

00:15:49.919 --> 00:15:51.795
Winner. Pay the line.

00:15:55.006 --> 00:15:56.757
Yeah.

00:15:58.049 --> 00:15:59.884
Where are we doing this?

00:16:00.884 --> 00:16:04.512
No, I'm at the Hard Rock, of all places.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.929
Fine.

00:16:06.138 --> 00:16:07.514
I'm on my cell.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:11.891
- So where's the party?
- There is no party, just a quiet dinner.

00:16:12.058 --> 00:16:14.601
Hey, have you figured out what
you're gonna do with the restaurant?

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:17.728
Not yet. You figured out
what you're gonna do with that money...

00:16:17.937 --> 00:16:19.563
...that I paid you for it?

00:16:19.771 --> 00:16:21.898
I'm putting all mine on the hard ways.

00:16:22.106 --> 00:16:24.983
Jimmy's gonna buy a house
for himself and Marissa.

00:16:26.359 --> 00:16:27.609
Really?

00:16:28.944 --> 00:16:32.446
Last time I talked to Marissa,
she was planning on moving in with us.

00:16:41.118 --> 00:16:43.786
- ever gonna stop being mad at me, Ada?

00:16:44.412 --> 00:16:48.289
I'm sorry, but does it strike anyone else
as tragic that the boys are in Las Vegas...

00:16:48.497 --> 00:16:52.166
...doing God knows what, while we sit
here watching The Valley marathon?

00:16:52.375 --> 00:16:55.293
Hey, it's Summ's favorite show, okay?

00:16:55.502 --> 00:16:56.961
Right, Summ?

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.504
- Are you crying?
- No.

00:17:01.255 --> 00:17:03.590
It's a sad episode.

00:17:07.009 --> 00:17:08.635
- She broke up with Seth.
- Coop.

00:17:08.844 --> 00:17:10.470
- What? Why?
- Her dad doesn't approve.

00:17:10.678 --> 00:17:11.970
- Coop.
- Please.

00:17:12.179 --> 00:17:15.181
You think my dad approves
of Jimmy Cooper? The man's a felon.

00:17:15.389 --> 00:17:16.598
No offense.

00:17:16.807 --> 00:17:19.684
Yeah, I know. Anyway,
my mom still doesn't approve of Ryan.

00:17:19.892 --> 00:17:22.519
It's like a rule. Your parents almost have
to disapprove.

00:17:22.727 --> 00:17:24.937
Otherwise, the sex isn't good.

00:17:25.437 --> 00:17:27.939
- Was that an over-share?
- Yeah. He kind of is my dad.

00:17:31.066 --> 00:17:32.275
Yeah, I'll get the door.

00:17:33.984 --> 00:17:35.443
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:17:35.652 --> 00:17:37.361
Can I talk to you?

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.279
Alone?

00:17:39.446 --> 00:17:42.281
- Let's move.
- Yeah.

00:17:44.949 --> 00:17:48.743
- You want me to get you a stripper?
- Not me. Julie.

00:17:48.952 --> 00:17:51.203
And I only ask because...

00:17:51.412 --> 00:17:53.788
...you were a stripper.
- Can I ask you something?

00:17:53.997 --> 00:17:56.457
- How did you get yourself into this?
- I wish I knew.

00:17:56.665 --> 00:17:59.000
Does she have a picture of you
wearing culottes?

00:17:59.208 --> 00:18:00.668
You don't even like Julie.

00:18:01.668 --> 00:18:02.919
Marissa's still here.

00:18:03.127 --> 00:18:04.587
And that's not entirely true.

00:18:04.753 --> 00:18:06.129
You let her walk all over you.

00:18:06.338 --> 00:18:08.214
You're upset
because she's marrying Dad.

00:18:08.422 --> 00:18:11.258
Yeah, for his money.
Same reason that she married Jimmy.

00:18:11.591 --> 00:18:13.759
Well, she's not your biggest fan either.

00:18:13.968 --> 00:18:15.635
So why am I getting her a stripper?

00:18:15.844 --> 00:18:17.762
Because if you don't...

00:18:18.262 --> 00:18:21.431
...she's gonna make me take her
to a place called The Petting Zoo...

00:18:21.639 --> 00:18:24.599
...which, according to Todd
in Accounting, they pet.

00:18:25.516 --> 00:18:27.101
You know what? I'll do it.

00:18:27.976 --> 00:18:30.061
If Julie Cooper wants a stripper...

00:18:30.269 --> 00:18:32.062
...I know just the man for the job.

00:18:32.479 --> 00:18:34.272
Thank you.

00:18:46.530 --> 00:18:50.240
We live in an age of miracles. Look at
them frolic. Look how much fun that is.

00:18:50.449 --> 00:18:51.908
Bowling alleys in the penthouse.

00:18:52.116 --> 00:18:56.077
You know what I'm saying? Hotel rooms?
Beaches in the middle of the desert.

00:18:56.286 --> 00:19:00.914
There's so many bikini-clad women,
I haven't thought about Summer since...

00:19:01.122 --> 00:19:03.040
Since you left a message
on her machine?

00:19:03.248 --> 00:19:04.791
Sure, but that was 20 minutes ago.

00:19:04.999 --> 00:19:07.084
I'm feeling liberated now. Confident.

00:19:07.293 --> 00:19:10.378
Like I could walk up to any one
of these women and just...

00:19:10.586 --> 00:19:12.129
...converse.

00:19:12.337 --> 00:19:13.546
Know what I'm saying?

00:19:13.755 --> 00:19:15.423
Great, go for it.

00:19:18.883 --> 00:19:20.968
The thing is,
I don't want to be rude to you.

00:19:21.176 --> 00:19:22.761
- I can take care of myself.
- Yeah.

00:19:22.969 --> 00:19:26.721
But I can't. I can't just go up
to a strange girl and say...

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.223
Excuse me.
Would you mind if I kissed you?

00:19:29.431 --> 00:19:30.891
Are you talking to me?

00:19:36.561 --> 00:19:38.395
Sorry. The Hard Rock's kind of exclusive.

00:19:38.604 --> 00:19:41.898
You can't use the beach
unless you're with a guest, so I'm Jenn.

00:19:42.106 --> 00:19:44.024
- Seth.
- And you are an excellent kisser.

00:19:44.232 --> 00:19:46.734
Can I buy you guys a drink? Say thanks.

00:19:47.359 --> 00:19:49.736
Yeah, I think we're out, so that...

00:19:49.944 --> 00:19:51.904
Could you hold on one second?
It's Summer.

00:19:52.613 --> 00:19:54.697
- Hey.
- Cohen.

00:19:55.281 --> 00:19:57.282
- Listen, I've been thinking.
- Yeah.

00:19:58.199 --> 00:19:59.909
Hey, I have to kiss you again.

00:20:00.117 --> 00:20:01.743
- What?
- What?

00:20:03.286 --> 00:20:05.537
Cohen? What is going on over there?

00:20:07.288 --> 00:20:09.081
You're an amazing kisser.

00:20:10.123 --> 00:20:12.708
Hold that thought, please. Hey, Summer.

00:20:13.334 --> 00:20:15.418
- Hello?
- He's kissing another girl.

00:20:15.919 --> 00:20:18.879
Yes. Right in front of me on the phone.
I can't believe this.

00:20:19.087 --> 00:20:23.048
I have been crying actual tears
over that ass, and he's kissing randoms.

00:20:23.257 --> 00:20:25.925
Okay, you know what?
We're gonna have a girls' night out.

00:20:26.134 --> 00:20:28.510
Theresa's coming over.
We can do whatever you want.

00:20:28.885 --> 00:20:33.388
Really? Because all I want to do right now
is go to Las Vegas and kick Cohen's ass.

00:20:33.596 --> 00:20:35.348
- She's gonna kick my ass.
- Yeah.

00:20:35.556 --> 00:20:38.558
- Was that your girlfriend?
- "Was" being the operative word there.

00:20:38.766 --> 00:20:40.351
I'm so sorry. I should go.

00:20:40.559 --> 00:20:43.936
I shouldn't even be here. I should go.
I have a paper to write, anyway.

00:20:44.145 --> 00:20:47.230
- Yeah, we should probably go too, so...
- Where are you guys headed?

00:20:47.438 --> 00:20:49.690
- Can I give you a lift?
- You have a car here?

00:20:50.107 --> 00:20:51.816
I live here. I go to UNLV.

00:20:52.692 --> 00:20:55.694
English major.
With a weakness for fake beaches.

00:20:55.902 --> 00:20:57.195
What about you guys?

00:20:57.862 --> 00:20:59.238
- Just visiting.
- Yeah.

00:20:59.404 --> 00:21:02.156
- We're looking for a blackjack game.
- It's sort of business.

00:21:02.364 --> 00:21:03.657
I don't know about blackjack...

00:21:03.865 --> 00:21:06.701
...but a couple of guys from my class
are doing this poker thing.

00:21:06.909 --> 00:21:08.368
It's a kind of intense, though.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:10.620
Wanna go?

00:21:10.786 --> 00:21:12.329
- Sure.
- Sure.

00:21:23.044 --> 00:21:24.712
- Hey.
- How'd it go with Caleb?

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.463
He stonewalled me. I got nothing.

00:21:27.672 --> 00:21:30.382
Maybe he's just out here
for his bachelor party.

00:21:30.549 --> 00:21:32.008
Yeah, right. A bachelor party...

00:21:32.216 --> 00:21:34.426
...where Robert Campbell
just happened to stop by...

00:21:34.635 --> 00:21:37.303
...and pay him half a billion dollars
for the coastline.

00:21:37.470 --> 00:21:40.680
So he's profiting from our loss.
He's Caleb Nichol.

00:21:40.889 --> 00:21:44.349
That's what he does. He paid us a huge
amount of money for that restaurant.

00:21:44.558 --> 00:21:47.976
- He's the reason I could bid on a house.
- You may want to retract that bid...

00:21:48.185 --> 00:21:51.187
...because according to Caleb,
Marissa's moving in with him.

00:21:54.647 --> 00:21:57.190
Summer had to go home,
but she wants us to call if we go out.

00:21:57.607 --> 00:21:59.817
I don't feel like going out much,
if that's okay.

00:22:00.026 --> 00:22:02.610
Yeah. No, of course it's okay.
We'll just order in.

00:22:02.819 --> 00:22:05.571
You want, like, Indian? Chinese? Sushi?

00:22:05.737 --> 00:22:07.864
No, not sushi. I can't do raw fish.

00:22:08.072 --> 00:22:10.741
Okay. Well, what about
something else to drink?

00:22:10.907 --> 00:22:13.701
I think we have, like, juice, soda...
Beer?

00:22:13.909 --> 00:22:15.285
No, I can't.

00:22:15.452 --> 00:22:17.036
I mean, I shouldn't. Thanks.

00:22:17.453 --> 00:22:21.998
You can't drink, you can't have sushi.
What, are you pregnant?

00:22:24.124 --> 00:22:25.583
Oh, my God. Are you pregnant?

00:22:48.723 --> 00:22:50.849
- We're just playing Texas Hold'em, right?
- Yep.

00:22:51.057 --> 00:22:53.476
Last time I was here,
it was, like, a 250 buy-in.

00:22:53.684 --> 00:22:55.727
As in $250?

00:22:55.935 --> 00:22:57.145
Why, you play?

00:22:57.353 --> 00:22:58.520
Yeah, just for fun.

00:22:58.729 --> 00:23:01.272
Well, it was fun,
until last time I lost that 250.

00:23:06.525 --> 00:23:09.277
These guys, they don't play for fun.

00:23:17.532 --> 00:23:19.617
- You do know how to play poker, right?
- Yeah.

00:23:19.825 --> 00:23:22.660
I haven't played in a while, but...

00:23:22.869 --> 00:23:25.537
- How about I go buy us a drink.
- Okay.

00:23:28.372 --> 00:23:31.333
- Look, we don't have to do this.
- Yeah, well, what about Theresa?

00:23:31.541 --> 00:23:34.668
- Theresa's not your responsibility.
- Not yours either, yet here we are.

00:23:34.876 --> 00:23:36.002
So listen...

00:23:36.211 --> 00:23:39.796
...I love the Vegas.
It's time to see if the Vegas loves me.

00:23:52.012 --> 00:23:53.221
Howdy.

00:23:59.058 --> 00:24:00.309
I haven't told anyone.

00:24:01.143 --> 00:24:03.978
Not my mom. Not Eddie.

00:24:04.145 --> 00:24:07.605
Especially not Ryan.
You're the only one who knows, so...

00:24:07.814 --> 00:24:09.648
I'm not gonna tell anyone.
I promise.

00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:15.860
- Do you not want to talk about this?
- I've been going crazy keeping it to myself.

00:24:17.653 --> 00:24:20.113
Okay. So do you know
what you want to do?

00:24:20.488 --> 00:24:23.532
I don't even have the money
to get to Atlanta...

00:24:23.740 --> 00:24:28.994
...so I have no idea
how I would pay for an...

00:24:34.330 --> 00:24:36.748
I mean, even if I had the baby...

00:24:37.832 --> 00:24:41.793
...I work in a bakery.
You know, what am I supposed to do?

00:24:42.669 --> 00:24:45.796
- Well, maybe if you talked to Eddie...
- No, I can't.

00:24:46.338 --> 00:24:49.465
He'll try to convince me to marry him
and have the baby.

00:24:51.341 --> 00:24:54.468
- Or else he'll say it isn't his.
- Who else's could it be?

00:25:40.830 --> 00:25:42.831
All in.

00:25:43.499 --> 00:25:45.125
Twenty-five hundred.

00:26:02.927 --> 00:26:04.512
Pocket aces.

00:26:15.310 --> 00:26:17.395
Hey, how you doing there, buddy?

00:26:17.603 --> 00:26:20.480
We got your bar mitzvah money,
Theresa's money. Now we gotta go.

00:26:20.688 --> 00:26:23.565
No. What about the Ryan-and-Seth-
going-to-Europe money, my man?

00:26:23.774 --> 00:26:26.108
- Get back in there. We can get Vespas.
- Vespas?

00:26:26.317 --> 00:26:27.860
Yeah, it's Europe.

00:26:28.026 --> 00:26:31.320
Harleys. I don't know. The point is,
why quit when you're ahead?

00:26:31.529 --> 00:26:34.739
If we don't, Angry Trucker Hat
over there is gonna hurt me.

00:26:35.489 --> 00:26:36.740
Maybe he's not angry at you.

00:26:36.949 --> 00:26:39.700
He's angry because he found out
people don't wear trucker hats anymore.

00:26:39.909 --> 00:26:42.202
Come on.
I'm doing so good with Jenn, I think.

00:26:42.410 --> 00:26:44.078
Invite her back to the hotel room.

00:26:44.287 --> 00:26:48.414
It is kind of sweaty in here. I'd like
to do that. But how am I gonna do that?

00:26:49.415 --> 00:26:50.624
Hey.

00:26:50.832 --> 00:26:53.084
So, Seth and I were wondering...

00:26:54.334 --> 00:26:57.586
...if...
- lf you would come to our hotel room...

00:26:57.795 --> 00:27:00.463
...and go bowling,
which is not as weird as it sounds.

00:27:00.630 --> 00:27:02.506
Are you guys staying in the penthouse?

00:27:02.715 --> 00:27:06.801
My girlfriends and I have always wanted to
rent that for a night, but it's so expensive.

00:27:07.551 --> 00:27:11.012
Yeah, well, you should call them.
You should bring them over.

00:27:11.929 --> 00:27:13.847
- Are you serious?
- Yeah. Call them.

00:27:14.055 --> 00:27:15.514
Okay. Thanks.

00:27:31.107 --> 00:27:34.151
Now, isn't this better
than some seedy Hollywood club?

00:27:36.277 --> 00:27:37.820
When's the stripper getting here?

00:27:38.028 --> 00:27:40.530
Don't tell me.
I want it to be a surprise.

00:27:42.239 --> 00:27:44.491
- Surprise.
- I'll get it.

00:27:44.699 --> 00:27:47.826
Maybe I better go with you.
You know...

00:27:48.035 --> 00:27:51.037
...in case it's a UPS man
and I have to sign for the package.

00:27:51.245 --> 00:27:54.789
Or maybe it's a plumber
and he needs to tighten my pipes.

00:27:54.997 --> 00:27:58.541
Or, you know what, what if it's...?
Hailey.

00:27:59.083 --> 00:28:02.919
- What are you doing here?
- Kirsten invited me, since you forgot.

00:28:03.127 --> 00:28:04.587
My memory's fine.

00:28:04.795 --> 00:28:06.421
- Crab cakes.
- I can't stay.

00:28:06.630 --> 00:28:09.506
I saw a fire truck out front and wanted
to make sure everything was okay.

00:28:09.715 --> 00:28:11.174
Fire truck?

00:28:12.508 --> 00:28:13.884
Is it hot in here?

00:28:15.677 --> 00:28:17.220
Or is it just me?

00:28:41.735 --> 00:28:44.695
Hailey, I said one stripper.

00:29:08.085 --> 00:29:09.878
- Hello?
- Hey.

00:29:10.086 --> 00:29:11.295
Thank God it's you.

00:29:11.504 --> 00:29:15.840
There are four male strippers dressed
as firemen dancing in our living room.

00:29:16.048 --> 00:29:17.966
Theme stripping, you gotta love that.

00:29:20.593 --> 00:29:21.802
Oh, wait.

00:29:22.010 --> 00:29:24.303
Now they're not dressed
as anything at all.

00:29:24.512 --> 00:29:26.179
Try to keep them off the furniture.

00:29:26.388 --> 00:29:28.389
So how's everything going in Vegas?

00:29:28.598 --> 00:29:31.683
Let me ask you something.
Do you find it odd that after your father...

00:29:31.891 --> 00:29:34.726
...bought into the restaurant,
as powerful as he is...

00:29:34.893 --> 00:29:36.644
...we were still denied our liquor license?

00:29:36.853 --> 00:29:40.897
Yeah, but the guy that was on the liquor
board was an ex-client of Jimmy's.

00:29:41.064 --> 00:29:43.482
So your dad doesn't know anyone
on the liquor board?

00:29:43.690 --> 00:29:46.567
He knows everyone. But why
would he do something like that?

00:29:46.776 --> 00:29:48.360
He was a partner in the restaurant.

00:29:48.568 --> 00:29:51.945
So he could buy us out cheap, turn
around and sell it to Robert Campbell...

00:29:52.154 --> 00:29:53.321
...for 10 times as much.

00:29:54.530 --> 00:29:55.990
Sandy, he wouldn't do that.

00:29:56.156 --> 00:29:59.659
Honey, when are you gonna realize
there is nothing your dad wouldn't do?

00:29:59.867 --> 00:30:02.911
- Well, what are you gonna do?
- I'm gonna talk to your father.

00:30:03.619 --> 00:30:05.371
- Hey, Ryan.
- Yeah.

00:30:06.121 --> 00:30:07.330
I'm proud of you, man.

00:30:07.539 --> 00:30:09.540
Not as proud
as if we were on Vespas, but...

00:30:09.748 --> 00:30:11.833
- Right.
- Jenn, we're gonna do strip bowling.

00:30:12.041 --> 00:30:14.793
I'm not a very good bowler,
so you'll probably see my tush.

00:30:15.377 --> 00:30:17.128
Go ahead.
I'm gonna catch up. All right?

00:30:17.336 --> 00:30:18.962
- Yeah. Hurry up.
- Okay.

00:30:21.547 --> 00:30:23.507
Hey, I still haven't heard from you.

00:30:23.715 --> 00:30:26.926
Just want to make sure you're okay.
Ryan's here. He'd like to say hi...

00:30:27.134 --> 00:30:30.094
...so give us a call back, okay?
Love you, kiddo.

00:30:30.678 --> 00:30:32.638
Been calling all day.
She hasn't picked up.

00:30:32.846 --> 00:30:34.139
Everything okay?

00:30:34.347 --> 00:30:39.183
Listen. Do you know anything about
Marissa moving in with Caleb and Julie?

00:30:40.184 --> 00:30:41.643
Yeah.

00:30:42.394 --> 00:30:45.312
- She finally told you?
- No, she didn't.

00:30:46.354 --> 00:30:49.398
Caleb told Sandy.
Is there something I should know?

00:30:50.565 --> 00:30:52.317
What?

00:30:52.525 --> 00:30:55.360
Nothing. I just don't know why
he'd do that. They had a deal.

00:30:55.819 --> 00:30:57.278
Deal?

00:30:57.445 --> 00:30:59.446
What kind of deal?

00:31:04.032 --> 00:31:05.408
Move.

00:31:05.617 --> 00:31:09.827
Hi. The name is Cohen. C-O-H-E-N.
I think that's how you spell it.

00:31:11.704 --> 00:31:15.122
You can pretty much see
the entire strip from here.

00:31:16.415 --> 00:31:19.083
Yeah. You can see it from here too.

00:31:24.086 --> 00:31:25.295
It's very impressive.

00:31:26.505 --> 00:31:28.798
Wait till you see what happens next.

00:31:29.173 --> 00:31:32.550
I would, actually. I would like that
very much, to see what happens next.

00:31:32.758 --> 00:31:36.803
The thing is, I'm kind of in love with
my girlfriend, and that makes it weird.

00:31:36.969 --> 00:31:39.971
- Ex-girlfriend. Right?
- That's a good point.

00:31:48.185 --> 00:31:49.978
Cohen!

00:31:50.394 --> 00:31:53.146
